## 1. Introduction
Crystalline Nanoporous Framework Materials (CNFMs) have formed an integral part of both academic and industrial materials science over the past half a century. It is the nanometer length scale of the pores within these materials, together with the ability to modify and functionalize their structural frameworks which continue to hold both
